GIF is now refused in /add, @path and --image, and every "supported formats" message reads from one list. It's committed as 1357e1e5, titled Fixes #1143. Clippy, fmt and the full cargo test run all pass.

What I chose (option (a) on #1143): refuse GIF everywhere, the same way yoagent 0.27.1's own read_file does. The user-facing reason: an image that only Anthropic accepts stops working mid-conversation as soon as the provider changes (/provider, a fallback model, a config edit). The cost is that Anthropic users can no longer attach GIFs; the refusal message tells them to convert to PNG. I didn't build per-provider acceptance (option b): it would need the provider passed into /add and @path, and it would keep exactly the accept-now, fail-later behaviour that is the bug. The commit says this.

Changes:
• The list: gif is gone from SUPPORTED_IMAGE_FORMATS, and its doc comment now says why, with the date.
• Refused formats: a new REFUSED_IMAGE_EXTENSIONS copies yoagent's private refused list by hand (gif, bmp, tif, tiff, heic, heif, avif, ico, jxl), so each gets a reason and a conversion hint.
  • Beyond the task: the task only named GIF. Taking yoagent's whole list was free, and BMP and the rest used to fall through to the text reader and fail with a confusing UTF-8 error.
• One joiner: the --image error and the --help line now read supported_image_extensions(). Both used to have their own typed copy, and both still listed bmp, which had already been removed from the list (#698).

Checked with the built binary on a real 1×1 GIF in a temp dir:
• -p hi --image dot.gif exits 1 with: `error: dot.gif: GIF images are not attached (the model's read_file and several providers refuse them; supported: png, jpg, jpeg, webp). Convert it to PNG first…`
• --image notes.txt exits 1 with: error: 'notes.txt' is not a supported image format. Supported: png, jpg, jpeg, webp
• In the REPL, /add dot.gif and see @dot.gif print the same ✗ line, nothing is attached, and the @mention stays as typed.
• --help shows (png, jpg, jpeg, webp;

Tests: the three tests that pinned GIF being accepted are now refusal tests, not deleted. New tests cover:
• the refusal wording;
• near-misses that must not be refused: a.png, a.WEBP, gif.rs, Makefile, x.gif/notes, and an empty path;
• handle_add and expand_file_mentions on a real gif file;
• the help text containing exactly the list's formats and no "gif".

Sizes: the task asked for commands_file.rs to shrink or hold, and it didn't: it grew 2854 → 2936 (+82). I updated its entry in tests/module_size.rs with the reason. cli.rs shrank by 1 line because the --image message moved out of it.

The .gif entry in commands_search.rs's binary-extension list stays: that list means "don't search inside this file", which is a different thing.
